# Drafted by Gemini (R25 endings), edited.

~ start
Narrator: The clocktower in Wickermoor strikes its final hour, and the bronze bell cracks in the stillness before the echo can fade.
Narrator: Above the valley, the gargantuan crescent moon fills the whole of the heaven, so close that the frost on its stone chills your faces.
Narrator: No wind stirs the heather on the moor, and no bird calls from the dark boughs of the Wytchwood.
Narrator: The pale crone's face fills the sky from hill to hill, blotting out the last cold stars.
Narrator: Then the sky comes down, and the stone meets the earth in a blinding white hush.
Narrator: After the dust settles across the hollow, there is no village, no forest, and no track left in the dark.
-> END
